{"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Quick start","modules":[{"name":"SwiftCrossUI"}],"role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This quick start guide uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Although not strictly required, it simplifies many aspects of cross-platform distribution and provides a platform-agnostic configuration format for specifying things such as app icons and custom URL schemes.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’re new to Swift, we recommend starting with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"text":"Installing Swift Bundler","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Installing-Swift-Bundler"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Follow ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler?tab=readme-ov-file#installation-","type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"mint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the preferred installation method on macOS and Linux as of the last update to this quick start guide.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Installing system dependencies","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Installing-system-dependencies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each backend has different requirements. In this guide we’ll use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/DefaultBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" which uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" on macOS, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" on Linux, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/WinUIBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" on Windows, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" on iOS\/tvOS. Click through the backend relevant to your machine for detailed installation requirements. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","type":"reference"},{"text":" have no system dependencies.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Using Swift Bundler’s SwiftCrossUI template","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Using-Swift-Bundlers-SwiftCrossUI-template"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Bundler provides many built-in templates; we’ll use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCrossUI"},{"type":"text","text":" template. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCrossUI"},{"type":"text","text":" template uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultBackend"},{"type":"text","text":" to select the most appropriate backend at compile time."}]},{"code":["swift bundler create HelloWorld --template SwiftCrossUI","cd HelloWorld"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Running your app","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Running-your-app"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Running your new app with Swift Bundler is as simple as it gets!"}]},{"code":["swift bundler run"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS you can provide the "},{"code":"--device <device_name_or_id>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" option to run the app on a connected iOS or tvOS device, or the "},{"code":"--simulator <simulator_name_or_id>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" option to run the app in a simulator."}]},{"code":["# You can use any substring of the target device name. For example,","# \"iPhone\" matches any device connected with \"iPhone\" in its name.","swift bundler run --device \"iPhone\"","swift bundler run --simulator \"iPhone 15\""],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Making a change","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Making-a-change"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Open ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sources\/HelloWorld\/HelloWorldApp.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in an editor of your choosing. Change ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"Hello, World!\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"Hello, Earth!\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Repeat the previous step to verify that your changes get reflected.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"All done","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"All-done"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You’re good to go! If you make something cool with SwiftCrossUI let us know so we can add your project to our showcase once the SwiftCrossUI website is up and running!","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Getting Started","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-virtual-development-environment","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Examples","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Hot-reloading"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Getting-Started"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creating a cross-platform SwiftCrossUI app with Swift Bundler.","type"